    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d864-a3">

                <pb facs="0999" n="905" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg905"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No.
                    856—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Tevfik Pasha to Mr.
                            Riddle.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sublime Porte</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Ministry of Foreign
                                Affairs</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-04-09"><hi rendition="#italic">April 9,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chargé d’Affaires</hi>: In reply to the note, No.
                    121, which you addressed me on the 7th instant, I hasten to inform you that Mr.
                    Knapp has not been a prisoner (détenue), and that, if the Imperial authorities
                    have given him an escort on his voyage, it was precisely in order to insure his
                    safety. At Diarbekir he was the guest of the governor-general, and on his
                    arrival at Alexandretta he will be delivered up to the United States consul in
                    that town.</p>
                <p>Receive, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tevfik.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
